\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Brightly beams our Father's mercy
\par From His lighthouse evermore;
\par But to us He gives the keeping
\par Of the lights along the shore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Let the lower lights be burning,
\par Send a gleam across the wave;
\par Some poor fainting, struggling scaman
\par You may rescue, you may save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Dark the night of sin has settled,
\par Loud the angry billows roar;
\par Eager eyes are watching, longing,
\par For the lights along the shore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Let the lower lights be burning,
\par Send a gleam across the wave;
\par Some poor fainting, struggling scaman
\par You may rescue, you may save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Trim your feeble lamp, my brother,
\par Some poor sailor tempest- tossed,
\par Trying now to make the harbour,
\par In the darkness may be lost.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Let the lower lights be burning,
\par Send a gleam across the wave;
\par Some poor fainting, struggling scaman
\par You may rescue, you may save.
\par \f1 
